1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
We'll be right back.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,240
Well, good morning, Canvas Church.

3
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:38,040
Thanks so much for joining us this morning.

4
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:41,900
Man, did my heart need to sing about the goodness of God this morning.

5
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:51,500
Super thankful for the worship team kind of preparing our hearts for everything that's going to happen in this room and in the lobby and through the rest of your day.

6
00:00:52,420 --> 00:01:06,100
The thing that we hold on to in having a personal relationship with God is that it's not just about what happens in here, but it's about every moment of our lives because God is present and active in our lives.

7
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,040
If you don't know me, my name is Ryan.

8
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:12,780
I am one of the pastors on staff here, and I am so glad that you have joined us.

9
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:19,820
At the beginning of the year, we kind of titled this loose series, God Only Knows.

10
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:26,600
As our church is kind of in a season of transition, I thought it would be good, rather than to plan out some long-term series,

11
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:34,240
that we would just kind of week by week seek the Lord, seek the Holy Spirit, ask what He would have for us to hear, and respond to that.

12
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:44,620
And if I'm being honest, since this is a church of real people with real lives, I am a planner, and I like to know what's going to happen weeks in advance.

13
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:50,340
And so this has been really challenging for me as I, each week, to say, God, what do you have for us?

14
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:54,000
What might you be teaching us this week?

15
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:03,300
And so it's been tough for me, but I am confident this morning that the Lord has led me to the passage that we're going to be studying for a really good purpose.

16
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:12,080
And if you remember, if you checked it out online, the last time I preached, the Lord led me to this really weird, obscure little letter in Philemon.

17
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:15,260
And it's not a well-known passage.

18
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:19,260
It's a passage where Paul's writing specifically to a couple of individuals.

19
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:27,400
And for whatever reason, the Lord has yet again led me to a weird, obscure little passage at the end of 2 Timothy,

20
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:30,740
where Paul's kind of saying goodbye to his friends.

21
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:32,060
It's kind of his final address.

22
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:39,960
And 2 Timothy is actually the last book that Paul is going to write before he dies for his faith.

23
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:47,060
And so we're going to kind of look at this letter, this weird, obscure conversation that he's having with a few of his friends right before he leaves.

24
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:54,280
And ultimately, I think we're going to see some wisdom about persevering through trials.

25
00:02:54,340 --> 00:03:02,180
It's a weird text, so let me read it so that you can begin to question how in the world I'm going to preach a 40-minute message through this strange passage.

26
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:04,400
I'll pray, and then we'll kind of get into it.

27
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,600
Does that sound good for everybody?

28
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,900
Good.

29
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:07,560
All right.

30
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,380
2 Timothy 4, starting in verse 9.

31
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:41,280
Paul says,

32
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,080
My papers.

33
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:47,000
Alexander the coppersmith did me much harm, but the Lord will judge him for what he has done.

34
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,200
Be careful of him, for he fought against everything we said.

35
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:55,600
The first time I was brought before the judge, no one came with me.

36
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,160
Everyone abandoned me.

37
00:03:57,160 --> 00:04:01,980
May it not be counted against them, but the Lord stood with me and he gave me strength

38
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:06,200
so that I might preach the good news in its entirety for all the Gentiles to hear.

39
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:08,540
And he rescued me from certain death.

40
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:12,440
Yes, and the Lord will deliver me from every evil attack

41
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:15,100
and will bring me safely into his heavenly kingdom.

42
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:17,640
All glory to God forever.

43
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:19,360
Amen. Let's pray.

44
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:26,880
Father, we are so thankful that we have a cloud of witnesses of other believers that have gone before us

45
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:32,600
that have suffered for the faith, that have persevered trials and tribulations and difficulties,

46
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:36,140
that have been led by the Spirit to write the Scriptures,

47
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:45,260
to give us insight into how difficult it can be to follow Jesus in the midst of persecution and difficulty.

48
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:49,340
This morning, Holy Spirit, I pray that you would be present and active in this room,

49
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:54,820
that you would be teaching us lessons about what we can do practically in our lives

50
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:57,520
to be a people that persevere through trials,

51
00:04:57,520 --> 00:05:04,620
to be a people that get to the end of our lives more in love with Jesus than we ever were before.

52
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:07,420
This is not something that comes naturally or easy.

53
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:11,720
This is a day-by-day relationship that we invest in.

54
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:14,300
And so, Holy Spirit, teach us each what we need to hear.

55
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:19,920
Bring to mind areas in our lives that are drawing us out of relationship with you.

56
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:24,420
And give us wisdom about ways that we can invest in our relationship with you this morning

57
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,180
for your glory and for our good.

58
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:27,980
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

59
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:28,860
Amen.

60
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:33,620
You want to follow along that weird passage with a lot of names and places.

61
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:36,180
It is in 2 Timothy, so you want to turn in there.

62
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:38,120
That's where we'll be this morning.

63
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:42,040
As you're turning there, I'd love to get some participation from the group.

64
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:44,180
How many mini-goth fans do we have in the room?

65
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,840
Anybody in here enjoys a game of mini-goth?

66
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:48,200
We've got some mini-goth fans in here.

67
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:53,680
Somehow, I find a way to work golf into my sermons a lot, so I'm sorry about that, but

68
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:54,240
here we are.

69
00:05:54,240 --> 00:06:00,480
Marissa's family specifically, my family, Marissa's family, we all love mini-goth, but Marissa's

70
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:03,220
family specifically, we are like obsessed with mini-goth.

71
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:07,200
And we go on vacation together every two years.

72
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:12,540
And my brother-in-law and the siblings, like, we play so much mini-goth.

73
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:16,380
I think at one point we played, like, 15 games of mini-goth in one week.

74
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:17,560
It was insane, right?

75
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:24,600
But, and because we're men, all the women in the room are going to understand here in a second,

76
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:27,660
my brother-in-law, we decided to make a competition, right?

77
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:30,500
Because, like, you can't just have fun doing games.

78
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,560
There has to be a competition.

79
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,760
There has to be a winner and a loser.

80
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:36,940
There may or may not have been money placed on the tournament overall.

81
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:42,200
But because it was a tournament, my brother-in-law and I, we would fight to go last.

82
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:46,840
Every time we would go to play mini-golf, we would fight to go last.

83
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:50,200
And the reason that we would fight to go last is because there's this principle when it comes

84
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:53,900
to putting in golf, it's called seeing the line, right?

85
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:58,400
And, like, the more people that go before you, the more you can learn from the terrain ahead.

86
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:02,400
You can learn, like, which way the ball is going to go, which hills there are on the course.

87
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:08,600
And the goal of the course, it's designed to try and keep you from getting to the hole, right?

88
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:12,880
Like, there's obstacles in the way, there's things, there's difficulties that are trying to keep you.

89
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:16,300
From finishing the hole well.

90
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:21,800
And when I think about that, I think about the Christian life.

91
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:28,740
Because, like, living on earth, we have really three natural enemies that keep us from finishing well.

92
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:34,900
We've got the world, the flesh, and the devil that are all trying to keep us from loving Jesus well

93
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,080
throughout our entire life.

94
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:37,840
That's kind of a normal setup.

95
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:44,180
But even on top of that, oftentimes we have situations and circumstances, difficulties, trials in our life.

96
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:52,080
And when you go mini golfing, every once in a while, usually one or two holes per course, there's, like, there's a chance for you to lose the ball.

97
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:52,840
Right?

98
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,760
Like, there's water.

99
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:57,840
There's, like, not every hole has these, like, massive difficulties.

100
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,340
Sometimes it's just pretty simple.

101
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:01,080
But every once in a while, you'll get to a hole.

102
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:05,980
And it's really beneficial that you get to go last in those situations.

103
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:07,600
Because you get to see what's going to happen.

104
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:11,320
You get to see all of the dangers and difficulties ahead.

105
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:23,900
And in this small, obscure passage in 2 Timothy, we get to look at how some of our brothers and sisters in Christ went through a really difficult time in their life.

106
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:25,180
A trial in their life.

107
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:26,600
And some of them were successful.

108
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:28,740
Some of them persevered through difficulty.

109
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:31,480
Some of them started well and ended well.

110
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:34,380
Some of them started poorly and ended well.

111
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:37,520
Some of them started well and ended poorly.

112
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:44,240
And as we get into this passage, I can't help but think of that famous passage in Hebrews that says,

113
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:52,340
Therefore, since we are surrounded by such a crowd of witnesses to this life of faith, let us strip off every weight that slows us down,

114
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:55,380
especially the sin that so easily traps us up.

115
00:08:55,380 --> 00:09:00,020
And let us run with endurance the race God has set before us.

116
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:06,800
And so my hope and my prayer for this message this morning is that we would learn from those who have gone before us.

117
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:11,420
That we can learn some really practical lessons about how they persevered through trials,

118
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:15,260
about the way that obstacles got them off track from following Jesus.

119
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:20,700
And ultimately, I boiled it down to four lessons for persevering trials.

120
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:28,600
I think from 2 Timothy 4, we can learn four lessons, four practical lessons for what it looks like to persevere trials.

121
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:33,660
And if we're just honest this morning, every single person in this room is going through a trial.

122
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:39,180
Like, the American existence has been a trial for the last two and a half years.

123
00:09:39,180 --> 00:09:45,160
Like, there's this low profile hum in the background of all of our lives.

124
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:47,580
We're all going through a difficult season.

125
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:52,180
But on top of that, that's led some of us into even more difficult trials.

126
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:58,000
Like, some of us have gotten through COVID and, like, our lives still kind of look like what they did two and a half years ago.

127
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:07,260
But some of us, man, this is just trial on top of trial, broken relationships, lost jobs, financial struggles.

128
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:11,200
Like, there's a lot of trials in this room this morning.

129
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:23,200
And what happens when we face trials, if we're not careful, like, real people, real lives, if we're being honest, what happens when we face trials is it's really tempting to get angry.

130
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:26,480
Anybody else get angry when they face trials?

131
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:29,000
Anybody else start to believe, like, I shouldn't be here?

132
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,860
I shouldn't be facing these situations?

133
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:34,000
Like, God, you shouldn't have let this happen to me?

134
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:40,560
And what happens when we get angry is the Scripture says that anger gives the devil a foothold in our lives.

135
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:43,480
Like, we get angry, we get bitter.

136
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:46,480
And when we get angry, we get bitter.

137
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:51,040
There's even more opportunity for us to get knocked off track.

138
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:58,560
And so I think now more than ever, it's so important for us to pay a close attention to how we're living, how we're persevering.

139
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:01,480
What does our relationship look like in the midst of this trial?

140
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:09,860
Because I was talking to somebody the other day, and I said, like, it feels like the last two and a half years is kind of like a snow vacation in school, right?

141
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:13,280
Because, like, life just changes every other week.

142
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:18,040
Like, we think we get into a pattern, we think we get into a rhythm, and then something else changes.

143
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:27,780
We're in a difficult season, and if we're not paying attention to the trajectory of our lives, it's really easy for us to look back six months from now and say,

144
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:32,280
wow, I never would have drawn up being here where I am.

145
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:34,800
But if we're not careful to pay attention to those things, we can get there.

146
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:41,360
So that's why, man, I think it's so important this morning that we learn from the lessons of these brothers and sisters who have gone before us.

147
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:44,460
And what they're facing in 2 Timothy is way worse than COVID, right?

148
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:46,460
Like, they're being persecuted for the faith.

149
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:52,720
Like, it's possible that they're going to give their lives for following Jesus.

150
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:55,640
So we're in similar situations.

151
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:58,600
They're in a more severe version of it.

152
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:03,500
And we get the first principle from these first couple of verses where Paul says,

153
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,360
Timothy, please come to me as soon as you can.

154
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,620
Why?

155
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:08,840
For Demas has deserted me.

156
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:10,220
Why did he leave?

157
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:14,260
Because he loves the things of this life.

158
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:19,060
So I think the first principle that we can learn for persevering through trials,

159
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:24,440
for having a life where we end up loving Jesus more at the end of it than at the beginning of it,

160
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:28,320
is that we have to keep a close eye on our affections.

161
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:36,580
It says Demas deserted Paul because he's in love with the things of this life.

162
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:39,140
See, Demas started out well.

163
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:43,600
At the end of that letter in Philemon chapter, or in Philemon verse 23 and 24,

164
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:47,440
it says that Demas and Luke are my fellow workers.

165
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:51,500
So prior to this, Paul is saying, like, Demas is a brother in Christ,

166
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:54,160
a fellow minister of the gospel.

167
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:59,020
Demas was at one point living well for the Lord, making a difference,

168
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:00,760
having a kingdom impact.

169
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:05,200
Demas started out as a faithful servant of God and a co-worker of Paul.

170
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:12,060
But somehow, through some difficulties and trials of following Jesus in the first century,

171
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:17,580
he ended up at a point where he was willing to totally walk away from his faith in Jesus

172
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:22,380
because he was in love with the things of this world.

173
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:25,020
And this doesn't happen overnight.

174
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:28,440
Like, those of us that are married, we know that this doesn't happen overnight.

175
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:31,980
You don't wake up the day after your honeymoon hating your spouse.

176
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:33,900
It doesn't happen.

177
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:35,760
Like, you get home from the honeymoon, everything's great.

178
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:36,420
Life's great.

179
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,060
Like, everything's great.

180
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:43,740
But, if we look at the divorce rate in our country, like, over time,

181
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:46,800
if people aren't careful, if people don't pay attention,

182
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:49,540
if they don't keep a close eye on their affections,

183
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:52,780
over time, they get to a point where they wake up and they say,

184
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:54,500
man, I don't know.

185
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,680
I don't know that I love this person anymore.

186
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:59,500
I don't know that this is going to work out anymore.

187
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:05,640
You don't have a radical encounter with the overwhelming, never-ending love of Jesus

188
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:09,220
and then the next day decide that he's no longer worth following.

189
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:17,860
But, over time, if we don't pay attention to the way that our souls are interacting with the things of this earth,

190
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:25,320
it's easy, sometimes more easy than not, to end up loving the things of this world

191
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:28,040
more than we love the giver of those good gifts,

192
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:30,220
more than we love Jesus himself.

193
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:32,880
And, if we're going to have a faith that perseveres,

194
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:37,200
we have to keep a close eye on the things that we love.

195
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:42,200
The best way I can illustrate this is oil changes.

196
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,080
Right?

197
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,040
Like, I was talking to somebody this week about this,

198
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:50,460
and the reality is, like, you can, and Brad and Mission Auto in the microchurch,

199
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,100
you guys are watching,

200
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:54,460
they're either going to love this illustration or hate this illustration.

201
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:57,040
But, I know nothing about cars.

202
00:14:57,700 --> 00:15:00,500
Pretty much the only thing I do for myself is change the oil,

203
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:03,360
and I don't do that in the winter because, you know,

204
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:05,940
what's an extra 20 bucks so that I can feel my fingers for a day?

205
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:10,600
But, so, here's the deal with oil changes, right?

206
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:15,360
Like, you can go a couple thousand miles over the time that you're supposed to get your oil changed,

207
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,460
and you're really not going to notice much of a difference.

208
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:22,840
Like, you're not going to fully see the effects that are happening to your engine.

209
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:26,720
And somebody else can get in your car, and they're not going to be like,

210
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:29,220
whoa, man, it feels like you need an oil change.

211
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,220
Right?

212
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:35,660
Like, you're not going to feel the effects of going a couple thousand miles over your oil change.

213
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:39,960
Nobody else around you is going to feel the effects of going a couple thousand miles over your oil change.

214
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:43,360
But if you go a couple thousand more, a couple thousand more, a couple thousand more,

215
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:45,720
it can be catastrophic.

216
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:54,180
I had a friend call me a couple years ago as his wife's car blew up, and she was in West Virginia.

217
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:58,260
And I guess he thought, like, I just knew everybody in West Virginia.

218
00:15:58,260 --> 00:16:03,920
I think that's kind of the common misconception about people from West Virginia is we either know everyone in West Virginia

