What are the odds?

453
00:29:28,140 --> 00:29:32,320
Like, shipwrecked twice and you're like, man, this is a bad day.

454
00:29:32,320 --> 00:29:33,220
But shipwrecked three times.

455
00:29:33,220 --> 00:29:38,340
And then he literally, like, made his way from a shipwreck onto a deserted island.

456
00:29:38,340 --> 00:29:41,640
Found a couple of natives there and was making a fire to warm himself.

457
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:45,440
And as he reached for the wood, a venomous snake bit him.

458
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:48,200
At that point, I'm like, God, no thank you.

459
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:49,000
Right?

460
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,080
Like, I am done.

461
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:52,020
I have persevered long enough.

462
00:29:52,020 --> 00:29:54,340
Three shipwrecks and now I'm bit by a snake.

463
00:29:54,340 --> 00:29:55,600
Peace out.

464
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:58,200
This is Paul's resume.

465
00:29:58,200 --> 00:30:02,720
And if anybody had the opportunity to say, I'm just going to coast for a time.

466
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:04,660
I'm going to move to Florida.

467
00:30:04,660 --> 00:30:08,920
Sit in a golf cart somewhere and eat Girl Scout cookies.

468
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:09,660
It was Paul.

469
00:30:09,660 --> 00:30:17,020
But at the end of it all, he's still in prison in a dark, cold prison cell.

470
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:24,280
And he says, bring me a coat, bring me my Bible, and bring me some paper because I'm going to finish my life well.

471
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:29,120
I'm going to encourage brothers and sisters in Christ that following Jesus is worth it.

472
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:35,440
Even in the midst of trials and difficulties, that if you end up falling in love with the things of this world,

473
00:30:35,440 --> 00:30:40,080
you're just selling your soul to something meaningless when God offered you something abundant.

474
00:30:40,620 --> 00:30:54,600
And it can be really easy for us to look at this and be like, yeah, but he's Paul.

475
00:30:54,600 --> 00:30:55,920
Right?

476
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:57,080
Like, he's an apostle.

477
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:58,900
So, like, he's supposed to be built different.

478
00:30:58,900 --> 00:31:01,600
He's supposed to have this extra measure of grace.

479
00:31:01,700 --> 00:31:03,160
Like, good for Paul for doing this.

480
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:04,120
I'm glad he did it.

481
00:31:04,120 --> 00:31:09,020
But if I get to a certain point where, like, it's just too hard, I'm going to give up on all that stuff.

482
00:31:09,020 --> 00:31:11,920
I'm just going to focus on, like, being alive.

483
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:13,140
Keeping my kids alive.

484
00:31:13,140 --> 00:31:13,500
Right?

485
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:19,680
And I often say this when we talk about, like, my parents' parents' generation.

486
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:21,340
Like, my grandparents' generation.

487
00:31:21,340 --> 00:31:23,460
The World War II generation.

488
00:31:23,460 --> 00:31:23,760
Right?

489
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:25,920
I often say, man, they're, like, they're built different.

490
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:31,200
I hear about some of the things they do about, like, Corey told me a story about this.

491
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:38,220
My neighbor who's in that generation who, Corey watched him literally sew his own, like, sew his own stitches.

492
00:31:38,220 --> 00:31:40,380
He cut his hand while he was building something.

493
00:31:40,380 --> 00:31:45,340
And he was, like, oh, I'm going to stitch myself up with a rusty needle on some string.

494
00:31:45,340 --> 00:31:45,640
Right?

495
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:47,740
Like, that's, like, that's the things that they do.

496
00:31:47,740 --> 00:31:49,500
And we hear about those things.

497
00:31:49,500 --> 00:31:51,100
We're, like, man, they were just built different.

498
00:31:51,100 --> 00:31:52,720
I said that this week to my wife.

499
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:54,280
And she corrected me.

500
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:55,000
She said, you know what?

501
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:56,800
I understand what you're saying.

502
00:31:56,800 --> 00:32:05,180
But I think, like, if we made the same decisions that they made, if we faced the same circumstances they made,

503
00:32:05,180 --> 00:32:09,700
or they faced and chose to persevere, like, I think what we have inside of us,

504
00:32:10,180 --> 00:32:11,560
it's the same thing they have inside of them.

505
00:32:11,560 --> 00:32:14,100
We just often choose to use it differently.

506
00:32:14,100 --> 00:32:17,900
And I think the same is true with Paul, right?

507
00:32:17,900 --> 00:32:20,980
Like, it's really easy for us to look at Paul and be like, yeah, he's just built different.

508
00:32:20,980 --> 00:32:26,540
No, like, he's just literally a broken sinner filled with the Holy Spirit.

509
00:32:26,540 --> 00:32:28,800
And that's us.

510
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:31,940
Like, we're broken sinners filled with the Holy Spirit.

511
00:32:31,940 --> 00:32:33,160
We can persevere.

512
00:32:33,580 --> 00:32:35,200
We can not make lame excuses.

513
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:43,520
And if any of us have any reason to make lame excuses, all of us have a reason to make a lame excuse in 2022.

514
00:32:43,520 --> 00:32:49,320
Like, God, this pandemic thing, like, it's been a while, and I'm tired.

515
00:32:51,960 --> 00:32:53,480
Life is hard.

516
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:55,280
Things are difficult.

517
00:32:55,280 --> 00:33:00,220
I will get back to you when I get a hold of whatever is happening down here.

518
00:33:00,220 --> 00:33:05,920
Man, but if we're going to persevere, if we're going to end our lives more in love with Jesus than we started,

519
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:09,060
I think we've got to be with people that say, you know what?

520
00:33:09,180 --> 00:33:09,860
Yeah, life's hard.

521
00:33:09,860 --> 00:33:10,840
Things are difficult.

522
00:33:10,840 --> 00:33:13,300
We're facing trial after trial after trial.

523
00:33:13,300 --> 00:33:17,980
But I'm going to keep coming back to the author and perfecter of my faith.

524
00:33:17,980 --> 00:33:20,200
I love how 2 Corinthians 12 says it.

525
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:23,920
God says, my grace is sufficient for you.

526
00:33:23,920 --> 00:33:27,200
My power is made perfect in weakness.

527
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:31,240
My power is made perfect in weakness.

528
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:40,500
God says, it's at the time when you think you have the most opportunity for an excuse that I can show up and do the most miraculous thing in your life.

529
00:33:40,500 --> 00:33:43,120
It's when you're at wit's end.

530
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:45,820
It's when you feel like there's no more hope for you.

531
00:33:45,820 --> 00:33:56,120
It's in that season, in that situation, that if you will humbly come to the feet of Jesus, that his power will be made perfect in your weakness.

532
00:33:56,120 --> 00:34:00,180
Faithful people choose to rely on God's strength rather than their own.

533
00:34:00,780 --> 00:34:06,860
Don't let lame excuses keep you from intentionally following God in the midst of difficult circumstances.

534
00:34:06,860 --> 00:34:12,700
God can use you the most when you feel the least capable or qualified.

535
00:34:12,700 --> 00:34:22,160
And oftentimes, it's when we have the most reason for an excuse that we need to acknowledge that.

536
00:34:22,160 --> 00:34:26,640
Find somebody next to us and lock arms with them and ask them for help and accountability.

537
00:34:28,640 --> 00:34:33,080
I just started working out with our worship leader, Donovan, and both of us are like, it's cold outside.

538
00:34:33,080 --> 00:34:36,260
We'll start working out when it's warm outside.

539
00:34:36,260 --> 00:34:40,660
And if it wasn't for Donovan, I would be waiting until it's warm outside.

540
00:34:41,220 --> 00:34:47,740
And I don't know this for a fact, but I think if it wasn't for me, he would also be waiting until it's warm outside.

541
00:34:47,740 --> 00:34:52,020
But because we both said, like, that's a lame excuse.

542
00:34:52,020 --> 00:34:56,060
That's keeping us from getting to the place that we want to be.

543
00:34:56,060 --> 00:34:58,480
Let's lock arms and do this thing together.

544
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:01,580
And then we can persevere through this trial together.

545
00:35:01,580 --> 00:35:03,360
Let's not be a people that make lame excuses.

546
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:06,280
Let's lock arms with our brothers and sisters in Christ around us.

547
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:11,020
And let's be intentional in those moments when we have the most opportunity to make an excuse.

548
00:35:11,020 --> 00:35:14,700
Let's trust God to provide for us in our weakness.

549
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:18,400
Last principle we have this morning.

550
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:22,140
Found in verse 16 through 18.

551
00:35:22,140 --> 00:35:23,720
Paul says,

552
00:35:23,720 --> 00:35:28,880
The first time I was brought before a judge, no one came with me.

553
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:31,260
Everyone abandoned me.

554
00:35:31,260 --> 00:35:33,760
That means even Luke.

555
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:34,880
Like, Luke is with him.

556
00:35:34,880 --> 00:35:35,960
An author of Scripture.

557
00:35:35,960 --> 00:35:36,880
A doctor.

558
00:35:36,880 --> 00:35:38,260
A powerful leader in the church.

559
00:35:38,260 --> 00:35:39,860
Even Luke abandoned Paul.

560
00:35:39,860 --> 00:35:41,020
But Paul says,

561
00:35:41,020 --> 00:35:47,980
The Lord stood with me and gave me strength so that I might preach the good news in its entirety for all the Gentiles to hear.

562
00:35:47,980 --> 00:35:51,220
And God rescued me from certain death.

563
00:35:51,220 --> 00:35:57,080
Yes, and the Lord will deliver me from every evil attack and will bring me safely into his heavenly kingdom.

564
00:35:57,080 --> 00:35:59,280
All glory to God forever.

565
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:00,580
Amen.

566
00:36:00,580 --> 00:36:08,140
I think the last principle we can learn if we're going to persevere through trials is not to let fear paralyze us.

567
00:36:10,320 --> 00:36:13,620
Paul was in prison for following Jesus.

568
00:36:13,620 --> 00:36:15,740
And he was going to trial.

569
00:36:15,740 --> 00:36:20,500
And he should have been killed for his faith the first time.

570
00:36:20,500 --> 00:36:23,520
There was no real reason for him not to be executed the first time.

571
00:36:23,520 --> 00:36:23,940
And he says,

572
00:36:23,940 --> 00:36:25,400
I came before the judge.

573
00:36:25,400 --> 00:36:29,540
And other brothers and sisters, they had the opportunity to have my back.

574
00:36:29,540 --> 00:36:32,140
They had the opportunity to show up.

575
00:36:32,140 --> 00:36:33,520
And they didn't.

576
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:37,320
And I can't help but think the only reason that they would not show up is out of fear.

577
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:38,860
Out of fear of what might happen to them.

578
00:36:38,860 --> 00:36:43,040
If they were associated with Paul who was on trial for being a Christian.

579
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:50,520
And I think for us as well, it's really easy for us to be afraid.

580
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:53,720
Be afraid of what other people might think about us.

581
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:57,860
Of how other people's opinions might view the way that we orient our lives.

582
00:36:57,940 --> 00:37:03,860
No one showed up at Paul's trial because they were afraid how it would negatively affect that they would be treated moving forward.

583
00:37:03,860 --> 00:37:08,500
And the early Christians definitely had a legitimate reason to be afraid.

584
00:37:10,500 --> 00:37:16,840
And how often do we shy away from living in such a way that honors God because we're afraid of what other people might think about us.

585
00:37:19,600 --> 00:37:22,640
We live in a culture that's increasingly anti-Christian.

586
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:26,520
And people are going to look at the way we orient our lives.

587
00:37:26,520 --> 00:37:28,740
At the way we handle our entertainment.

588
00:37:28,740 --> 00:37:31,260
At the way that we handle our screen time.

589
00:37:31,260 --> 00:37:35,700
At the way the decisions that we make that are going to ultimately lead us to fall more in love with Jesus.

590
00:37:35,700 --> 00:37:39,420
And people might think we're insane Mormons or Amish people.

591
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:41,000
Like that might happen.

592
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:44,340
We might be afraid of what other people might think about us.

593
00:37:44,340 --> 00:37:51,060
But don't let a fear of the judgment of others keep you from living in a way that will allow you to persevere through trials.

594
00:37:51,060 --> 00:37:56,780
See the incredible thing about nobody else showing up.

595
00:37:56,780 --> 00:38:01,900
As Paul says, when nobody else showed up, God did.

596
00:38:01,900 --> 00:38:03,920
God did.

597
00:38:03,920 --> 00:38:07,180
And God delivered me from the mouth of certain deaths.

598
00:38:07,260 --> 00:38:09,940
See, Paul thought for sure he was going to die after that first trial.

599
00:38:09,940 --> 00:38:14,180
He goes into that trial by himself.

600
00:38:14,180 --> 00:38:15,540
No one else around him.

601
00:38:15,540 --> 00:38:19,460
And he says, it was in that moment that God showed up.

602
00:38:19,460 --> 00:38:22,480
That God delivered me in a miraculous way.

603
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:29,600
And how often, how often do we miss out on God's provision in our life because we're too afraid to do the thing that he's calling us to do?

604
00:38:29,600 --> 00:38:36,620
How often are we like, you know what God, like I don't think I'm capable or able to do that thing that you're asking me to do.

605
00:38:36,620 --> 00:38:43,860
So by not going, we miss out on God showing up and giving us the strength to do the thing that he's calling us to do.

606
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:57,280
Second Corinthians 4 says, for this light momentary affliction, this trial on earth is preparing us for an eternal weight of glory beyond all comparison.

607
00:38:58,400 --> 00:39:03,700
We look not to the things that are seen, to the judgment of this world, but we look to the things that are unseen.

608
00:39:03,700 --> 00:39:08,860
So the things that are seen are transient, but the things that are unseen are eternal.

609
00:39:08,860 --> 00:39:13,360
There are things to be afraid of, but they can only hurt us so much.

610
00:39:13,360 --> 00:39:16,220
It can only provide temporary pain.

611
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:22,020
But if we persevere, if we seek to obey the Lord above everything else, the rewards are eternal.

612
00:39:22,020 --> 00:39:28,580
Paul saw God show up in an extraordinary way because he was faithful through his fears.

613
00:39:28,580 --> 00:39:33,740
Let's not let fear of this world keep us from focusing on eternal things.

614
00:39:36,740 --> 00:39:37,520
I'm almost done.

615
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:41,080
We're going to say communion together, but I hope this message is practical.

616
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:42,280
I hope it's encouraging.

617
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:49,440
My heart and my prayer for all of us at Canvas is that we would be a group of people that persevere well.

618
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:54,740
That we end up loving Jesus more at the end of our life than we did at the start.

619
00:39:54,740 --> 00:40:00,400
And I think some principles that we can learn from this passage are that if we just keep a close eye on our affections,

620
00:40:00,400 --> 00:40:10,560
if we pay attention to what we love and we build in practices that make us fall in love with Jesus more,

621
00:40:10,560 --> 00:40:14,900
that at the end of this thing we might be able to persevere through every trial and tribulation that we face.

622
00:40:14,900 --> 00:40:21,320
If we learn to learn from our past mistakes rather than to let them define us.

623
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:24,080
If we don't make lame excuses, if we don't let fear paralyze us.

624
00:40:24,080 --> 00:40:26,520
I think these are practical things that we can all learn from.

625
00:40:26,520 --> 00:40:30,040
But at the end of the day, these things are hard and we're going to fail.

626
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:32,220
Like we're going to fall short.

627
00:40:32,220 --> 00:40:36,180
So I want to end with another goth term.

628
00:40:36,180 --> 00:40:37,740
I'll teach everybody a goth term.

629
00:40:37,740 --> 00:40:38,560
It's called mulligan.

630
00:40:38,560 --> 00:40:42,580
Look to your neighbor if you're socially distancing and say mulligan.

631
00:40:42,580 --> 00:40:44,080
Mulligan.

632
00:40:44,080 --> 00:40:48,820
If you're not a golfer, you wouldn't maybe know this term.

633
00:40:48,820 --> 00:40:53,840
But the word mulligan is, it's a free stroke.

634
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:59,920
It's when a friend that's golfing with you sees how miserable you are at golf,

635
00:40:59,920 --> 00:41:04,340
sees how many mistakes you've made over and over and over again and they feel bad for you.

636
00:41:04,340 --> 00:41:05,480
And they say, you know what, man?

637
00:41:05,480 --> 00:41:06,080
Take a mulligan.

638
00:41:07,200 --> 00:41:08,940
And what a mulligan is, it's a free stroke.

639
00:41:08,940 --> 00:41:10,720
It doesn't show up on the scorecard.

640
00:41:10,720 --> 00:41:16,860
Mulligans are given to you by friends and they don't end up on the scorecard.

641
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:20,400
So if you're in here and you're like, Ryan, those principles are great,

642
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:29,080
but I've been not doing them well for so long that God's probably just so disappointed with me,

643
00:41:29,080 --> 00:41:30,900
angry with me, frustrated with me.

644
00:41:30,900 --> 00:41:34,520
And our God is a God of mulligan.

645
00:41:34,520 --> 00:41:40,560
Jesus is a friend who takes our mistakes off of the scorecard.

646
00:41:40,560 --> 00:41:42,860
2 Corinthians 5, verse 19 says,

647
00:41:42,940 --> 00:41:47,200
For God was in Christ reconciling the world to himself,

648
00:41:47,200 --> 00:41:53,540
mulliganing, no longer counting people's sins against them.

649
00:41:53,540 --> 00:41:55,820
Taking it off the scorecard.

650
00:41:55,820 --> 00:41:58,100
That's the gospel.

651
00:41:58,100 --> 00:42:00,920
That's the Jesus that we serve.

652
00:42:00,920 --> 00:42:03,980
He is a friend who takes our mistakes off the scorecard.

653
00:42:03,980 --> 00:42:09,360
I think about any of you in the room who have ever taught a toddler how to walk.

654
00:42:12,940 --> 00:42:15,560
I take a couple of steps and they fall.

655
00:42:15,560 --> 00:42:17,680
What do you do?

656
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:20,100
You say, how dare you?

657
00:42:20,100 --> 00:42:22,280
How hard is this walking thing?

658
00:42:22,280 --> 00:42:23,720
Can't you just figure it out already?

659
00:42:23,720 --> 00:42:25,300
No.

660
00:42:25,300 --> 00:42:30,100
You lovingly pick them up off the ground and they try again.

661
00:42:30,100 --> 00:42:35,140
And the next time they get a step or two further and the next time they get a step or two further

662
00:42:35,140 --> 00:42:38,680
and before you know it, they're like opening up the fridge and getting their own bowl of cereal.

663
00:42:39,940 --> 00:42:40,360
Right?

664
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:43,800
But each time they fall, each time they mess up,

665
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:46,900
the loving parent picks them up with grace and forgiveness.

666
00:42:46,900 --> 00:42:48,400
He says, try again.

667
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:52,160
And that's the God that we have.

668
00:42:52,160 --> 00:42:53,240
A loving God.

669
00:42:53,240 --> 00:42:55,560
Who every time we fall,

670
00:42:55,560 --> 00:42:59,660
doesn't look down with shame and condemnation and say,

671
00:42:59,660 --> 00:43:01,160
How dare you fall again?

672
00:43:01,160 --> 00:43:04,220
He says, just get up.

673
00:43:04,220 --> 00:43:05,160
Keep going.

674
00:43:05,160 --> 00:43:07,820
Keep walking.

675
00:43:08,880 --> 00:43:11,100
And if you just keep getting up and keep walking,

676
00:43:11,100 --> 00:43:12,960
I promise you,

677
00:43:12,960 --> 00:43:15,000
by the end of your life,

678
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:17,560
you'll be closer to Jesus than you were before.

679
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:18,800
By the end of your life,

680
00:43:18,800 --> 00:43:21,480
you can't even comprehend

681
00:43:21,480 --> 00:43:24,800
what you're able to persevere through

682
00:43:24,800 --> 00:43:26,120
with the strength of God.

683
00:43:26,120 --> 00:43:27,800
Like, there are trials ahead of you

684
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,880
that if I told you they were coming,

685
00:43:29,880 --> 00:43:31,560
you would just wave the white flag right now.

686
00:43:31,620 --> 00:43:32,600
But I promise,

687
00:43:32,600 --> 00:43:35,700
if you build into your life the practice

688
00:43:35,700 --> 00:43:36,720
of just getting up,

689
00:43:36,720 --> 00:43:38,100
trying again,

690
00:43:38,100 --> 00:43:39,660
coming back to the heart of the Father,

691
00:43:39,660 --> 00:43:40,680
every single time,

692
00:43:40,680 --> 00:43:41,940
you'll keep receiving grace,

693
00:43:41,940 --> 00:43:43,900
we'll keep giving you strength to move forward,

694
00:43:43,900 --> 00:43:45,640
and you can't even comprehend

695
00:43:45,640 --> 00:43:47,540
the things that you'll be able to get through

696
00:43:47,540 --> 00:43:48,640
with the strength of God

697
00:43:48,640 --> 00:43:50,460
if you just choose to obey Him.

698
00:43:52,780 --> 00:43:53,400
So man,

699
00:43:53,400 --> 00:43:55,320
what better reminder

700
00:43:55,320 --> 00:44:00,000
of the mulligan that Jesus provides us

701
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:01,280
than communion?

702
00:44:01,280 --> 00:44:03,700
Communion is a reminder each week

703
00:44:03,700 --> 00:44:04,340
that yes,

704
00:44:04,340 --> 00:44:05,840
we have made mistakes.

705
00:44:05,840 --> 00:44:07,740
We have hit balls out of bounds.

706
00:44:07,740 --> 00:44:09,580
We've hit balls into the water hazard.

707
00:44:09,580 --> 00:44:11,120
We have failed.

708
00:44:13,120 --> 00:44:15,500
Jesus does not count our failures against us.

709
00:44:15,500 --> 00:44:17,620
God actually counted all of our failures,

710
00:44:17,620 --> 00:44:19,260
past, present, and future,

711
00:44:19,260 --> 00:44:20,600
against Jesus.

712
00:44:20,600 --> 00:44:22,600
He took it on Himself.

713
00:44:22,600 --> 00:44:24,260
His body was broken.

714
00:44:24,260 --> 00:44:26,240
His blood was shed.

715
00:44:26,240 --> 00:44:30,100
So that we might persevere.

716
00:44:30,100 --> 00:44:33,300
So that we might just have endless grace

717
00:44:33,300 --> 00:44:35,840
to just keep giving up and moving forward.

718
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:40,940
We started with that famous verse in Hebrews.

719
00:44:40,940 --> 00:44:42,160
I want to finish with it.

720
00:44:42,340 --> 00:44:43,880
If you keep following it along,

721
00:44:43,880 --> 00:44:44,940
I think it's the perfect place

722
00:44:44,940 --> 00:44:45,820
to point us to communion.

723
00:44:45,820 --> 00:44:47,660
So therefore,

724
00:44:47,660 --> 00:44:48,540
since we are surrounded

725
00:44:48,540 --> 00:44:49,840
by a huge crowd of witnesses,

726
00:44:49,840 --> 00:44:50,860
the brothers and sisters

727
00:44:50,860 --> 00:44:51,940
who have gone before us,

728
00:44:51,940 --> 00:44:52,920
who have messed up

729
00:44:52,920 --> 00:44:53,700
and who have succeeded

730
00:44:53,700 --> 00:44:54,780
and who we can learn from,

731
00:44:54,780 --> 00:44:56,880
let us strip off every weight

732
00:44:56,880 --> 00:44:57,780
that slows us down,

733
00:44:57,780 --> 00:44:59,080
especially the sin

734
00:44:59,080 --> 00:45:00,640
that so easily trips us up.

735
00:45:00,640 --> 00:45:02,640
Let us run with endurance.

736
00:45:02,640 --> 00:45:04,380
There's that illustration there

737
00:45:04,380 --> 00:45:06,020
of us falling and getting back up

738
00:45:06,020 --> 00:45:07,380
and running with endurance

739
00:45:07,380 --> 00:45:09,320
the race that God has set before us.

740
00:45:09,320 --> 00:45:09,680
How?

741
00:45:09,680 --> 00:45:11,520
We do this by keeping

742
00:45:11,520 --> 00:45:13,320
our eyes on Jesus,

743
00:45:13,320 --> 00:45:15,740
the champion

744
00:45:15,740 --> 00:45:16,840
who initiates

745
00:45:16,840 --> 00:45:18,380
and perfects our faith

746
00:45:18,380 --> 00:45:22,100
because He endured the cross,

747
00:45:22,100 --> 00:45:23,580
disregarding its shame

748
00:45:23,580 --> 00:45:24,460
and now it's seated

749
00:45:24,460 --> 00:45:25,440
at the place of honor

750
00:45:25,440 --> 00:45:26,740
beside the throne.

751
00:45:26,740 --> 00:45:28,300
Think of all the hostility

752
00:45:28,300 --> 00:45:28,780
He endured.

753
00:45:28,780 --> 00:45:29,960
Think of our example of Jesus.

754
00:45:29,960 --> 00:45:30,920
His body broke

755
00:45:30,920 --> 00:45:32,220
and His blood shed.

756
00:45:32,220 --> 00:45:33,340
Think of what He endured

757
00:45:33,340 --> 00:45:34,400
for sinful people.

758
00:45:34,400 --> 00:45:37,900
And as you think about that,

759
00:45:37,900 --> 00:45:39,520
you'll persevere.

760
00:45:39,520 --> 00:45:40,900
You will not become weary

761
00:45:40,900 --> 00:45:41,840
and give up.

762
00:45:41,840 --> 00:45:43,300
After all,

763
00:45:43,300 --> 00:45:44,360
you have not yet

764
00:45:44,360 --> 00:45:46,400
given your lives

765
00:45:46,400 --> 00:45:47,780
in the struggle of sin.

766
00:45:48,920 --> 00:45:49,400
So,

767
00:45:49,400 --> 00:45:52,500
boil all of this stuff

768
00:45:52,500 --> 00:45:53,640
down into one sentence.

769
00:45:53,640 --> 00:45:55,700
Those who finish

770
00:45:55,700 --> 00:45:56,720
their lives faithfully,

771
00:45:56,720 --> 00:45:59,440
we're not ashamed

772
00:45:59,440 --> 00:46:00,380
to take a few mullings.

773
00:46:00,380 --> 00:46:02,160
And that's what communion

774
00:46:02,160 --> 00:46:03,120
is about each week.

775
00:46:03,120 --> 00:46:03,940
It's a reminder

776
00:46:03,940 --> 00:46:05,960
of how much we need

777
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:07,640
Jesus to pay the price

778
00:46:07,640 --> 00:46:08,720
for our sins.

779
00:46:08,720 --> 00:46:09,600
So,

780
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:10,860
if you're a believer

781
00:46:10,860 --> 00:46:11,300
in this room,

782
00:46:11,300 --> 00:46:11,920
I'd encourage you,

783
00:46:11,920 --> 00:46:13,140
let's take this wafer

784
00:46:13,140 --> 00:46:13,780
that represents

785
00:46:13,780 --> 00:46:15,020
the body of Christ

786
00:46:15,020 --> 00:46:15,620
broken through.

787
00:46:15,620 --> 00:46:24,780
Let's drink

788
00:46:24,780 --> 00:46:26,420
the juice

789
00:46:26,420 --> 00:46:26,980
that represents

790
00:46:26,980 --> 00:46:27,800
the blood of Christ

791
00:46:27,800 --> 00:46:28,480
shed for us.

792
00:46:28,480 --> 00:46:37,640
Let's pray.

793
00:46:37,640 --> 00:46:42,520
Father,

794
00:46:43,120 --> 00:46:46,460
life can get

795
00:46:46,460 --> 00:46:47,100
really difficult.

796
00:46:47,100 --> 00:46:50,940
Life on this earth

797
00:46:50,940 --> 00:46:51,940
is full of

798
00:46:51,940 --> 00:46:53,240
the results

799
00:46:53,240 --> 00:46:53,920
of sin.

800
00:46:53,920 --> 00:46:55,320
And it can be

801
00:46:55,320 --> 00:46:56,340
really easy for us

802
00:46:56,340 --> 00:46:57,500
to just get angry

803
00:46:57,500 --> 00:46:58,360
and tired

804
00:46:58,360 --> 00:47:00,420
and just give up.

805
00:47:00,420 --> 00:47:04,300
God,

806
00:47:04,300 --> 00:47:05,160
we're so thankful

807
00:47:05,160 --> 00:47:06,300
that you have given us

808
00:47:06,300 --> 00:47:07,580
every reminder

809
00:47:07,580 --> 00:47:08,540
and opportunity

810
00:47:08,540 --> 00:47:10,680
that when we fall,

811
00:47:10,680 --> 00:47:12,480
you're there

812
00:47:12,480 --> 00:47:13,360
to pick us up,

813
00:47:13,360 --> 00:47:14,540
to dust off

814
00:47:14,540 --> 00:47:15,700
our clothes

815
00:47:15,700 --> 00:47:16,420
and to help us

816
00:47:16,420 --> 00:47:17,380
take that next step

817
00:47:17,380 --> 00:47:18,160
forward.

818
00:47:18,160 --> 00:47:18,900
I pray that,

819
00:47:18,900 --> 00:47:19,500
God,

820
00:47:19,500 --> 00:47:20,300
we will be a people

821
00:47:20,300 --> 00:47:22,840
who learn

822
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:23,380
to just take

823
00:47:23,380 --> 00:47:24,040
an extra step

824
00:47:24,040 --> 00:47:24,660
each time.

825
00:47:24,660 --> 00:47:26,300
Get a little bit

826
00:47:26,300 --> 00:47:26,560
further

827
00:47:26,560 --> 00:47:27,180
and a little bit

828
00:47:27,180 --> 00:47:27,480
further

829
00:47:27,480 --> 00:47:28,160
and a little bit

830
00:47:28,160 --> 00:47:28,500
further.

831
00:47:28,500 --> 00:47:30,200
God,

832
00:47:30,200 --> 00:47:31,100
let us be a people

833
00:47:31,100 --> 00:47:33,760
that fix

834
00:47:33,760 --> 00:47:34,580
our eyes

835
00:47:34,580 --> 00:47:35,360
on Jesus,

836
00:47:35,360 --> 00:47:37,080
that receive

837
00:47:37,080 --> 00:47:37,580
forgiveness

838
00:47:37,580 --> 00:47:38,580
every time we feel

839
00:47:38,580 --> 00:47:40,340
that we come to you,

840
00:47:40,380 --> 00:47:41,440
confess our sins

841
00:47:41,440 --> 00:47:42,220
and you're faithful

842
00:47:42,220 --> 00:47:43,000
and just forgive

843
00:47:43,000 --> 00:47:43,440
our sins

844
00:47:43,440 --> 00:47:44,140
and to cleanse

845
00:47:44,140 --> 00:47:44,700
us from all

846
00:47:44,700 --> 00:47:45,440
unrighteousness.

847
00:47:45,440 --> 00:47:47,260
God,

848
00:47:47,260 --> 00:47:48,160
let us be a people

849
00:47:48,160 --> 00:47:49,820
that lock arms

850
00:47:49,820 --> 00:47:50,520
with one another,

851
00:47:50,520 --> 00:47:52,560
hold each other

852
00:47:52,560 --> 00:47:53,180
accountable,

853
00:47:53,180 --> 00:47:55,900
point each other

854
00:47:55,900 --> 00:47:56,940
to your faithfulness

855
00:47:56,940 --> 00:47:57,880
and your goodness

856
00:47:57,880 --> 00:47:58,980
in our life.

857
00:47:58,980 --> 00:47:59,900
And at the end

858
00:47:59,900 --> 00:48:01,120
of it all,

859
00:48:01,120 --> 00:48:01,300
God,

860
00:48:01,300 --> 00:48:02,100
let us be a people

861
00:48:02,100 --> 00:48:03,480
who know how good

862
00:48:03,480 --> 00:48:03,880
you are,

863
00:48:03,880 --> 00:48:05,780
who believe it

864
00:48:05,780 --> 00:48:06,720
with all of our hearts,

865
00:48:06,720 --> 00:48:08,320
who aren't tempted

866
00:48:08,320 --> 00:48:08,820
to think

867
00:48:08,820 --> 00:48:09,500
that this world

868
00:48:09,500 --> 00:48:10,040
has something

869
00:48:10,040 --> 00:48:10,900
better to offer.

870
00:48:10,900 --> 00:48:13,040
But who know

871
00:48:13,040 --> 00:48:15,200
that these light

872
00:48:15,200 --> 00:48:16,620
momentary afflictions

873
00:48:16,620 --> 00:48:18,300
are nothing

874
00:48:18,300 --> 00:48:19,120
to me compared

875
00:48:19,120 --> 00:48:20,460
to the eternal

876
00:48:20,460 --> 00:48:21,100
weight of glory

877
00:48:21,100 --> 00:48:21,560
that you have

878
00:48:21,560 --> 00:48:22,860
prepared for us

879
00:48:22,860 --> 00:48:23,680
in your kingdom.

880
00:48:23,680 --> 00:48:24,100
God,

881
00:48:24,100 --> 00:48:24,880
until that day

882
00:48:24,880 --> 00:48:25,280
comes,

883
00:48:25,280 --> 00:48:27,460
let us just be

884
00:48:27,460 --> 00:48:28,660
faithful representatives

885
00:48:28,660 --> 00:48:29,540
of your kingdom.

886
00:48:29,540 --> 00:48:31,880
Let us get to a place

887
00:48:31,880 --> 00:48:32,620
where we end

888
00:48:32,620 --> 00:48:33,920
our lives well

889
00:48:33,920 --> 00:48:34,740
and we stand

890
00:48:34,740 --> 00:48:35,540
before you

891
00:48:35,540 --> 00:48:36,380
and we hear

892
00:48:36,380 --> 00:48:36,980
your voice

893
00:48:36,980 --> 00:48:37,260
say,

894
00:48:37,260 --> 00:48:38,020
well done.

895
00:48:38,020 --> 00:48:40,760
Good and faithful

896
00:48:40,760 --> 00:48:41,940
son,

897
00:48:41,940 --> 00:48:43,220
daughter of the king,

898
00:48:43,220 --> 00:48:44,660
enter into the rest

899
00:48:44,660 --> 00:48:45,540
that I have prepared

900
00:48:45,540 --> 00:48:45,880
for you.

901
00:48:45,880 --> 00:48:49,140
In Jesus' name

902
00:48:49,140 --> 00:48:49,540
I pray.

903
00:48:49,540 --> 00:48:50,620
Amen.
